 training FLOPs vs reasoning performance comparison between Tina and baseline models. The calculation is detailed in Appendix A.\nFigure 4 :4Figure 4: Phase transition in LoRA-based RL. The raw data is from the Weights &amp; Biases training logs and smoothed via exponential moving average (EMA) with factor 0.1. The \"training turning point\" in the legend means the step where the format-like metrics (e.g., format reward, completion length) start to destabilize. Refer to Appendix E for the full set of plots.\nFigure 7 :7Figure 7: Phase transition in Tina-Open-RS3 and Tina-Open-RS3-GRPO. The raw data is from the Weights &amp; Biases training logs and smoothed via exponential moving average (EMA) with factor 0.1.\nTable 7 :7Performance evaluation of Tina-STILL-3-1.5B-preview.C hec kpo in t St ep s (3 740 S te ps per E poch) A IME 2 4 A IM E 2 5 A M C2 3 M ATH 5 0 0 GP QA M in erva Avg .50030.0013.3375.0083.6035.8632.3545.02100036.6720.0065.0084.8032.3227.9444.46150026.6720.0070.0083.8037.3726.8444.11200036.6730.0077.5084.6033.3326.8448.16250033.3330.0070.0083.0035.3527.5746.54300030.0020.0067.5082.6030.8125.7442.78350030.0026.6767.5082.2032.3226.1044.13C hec kpo in t St ep s (5 039 S te ps per E poch) A IME 2 4 A IM E 2 5 A M C2 3 M ATH 5 0 0 GP QA M in erva Avg .50030.0023.3367.5082.4039.3931.2545.65100043.3326.6767.5086.2037.8828.6848.38150030.0020.0080.0084.8032.8329.4146.17200020.0026.6757.5080.6029.2924.2639.72250013.3316.6752.5075.0031.3118.0134.47300026.6716.6757.5078.6028.7923.1638.57350023.3323.3362.5080.4031.8224.2640.94400020.0020.0070.0082.0041.4127.9443.56450023.3320.0072.5080.8034.8526.4742.99500020.0026.6775.0080.8033.3329.4144.20\nTable 8 :8Performance evaluation of Tina-DeepScaleR-1.5B-Preview.Ch eckpo i n t S te p s ( 8 75 St e p s p er E poc h ) AI M E 2 4 A I M E 25 A MC 23 M ATH5 00 GP QA M i ne rva Avg .5026.6723.3375.0084.2037.3729.0445.9410030.0030.0065.0083.0037.3729.7845.8615036.6716.6765.0084.8027.7827.9443.1420020.0026.6770.0083.8033.3327.94